From 65406abdf874f9c873ef7fe2da405c4de648d58d Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Kirill Mitrofanov <kmitrqq@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 22 Oct 2026 21:55:42 +0300
Subject: [PATCH 64/64] ASoC: qcom: audioreach: fix speaker protection VI
 channel map

The V/I feedback from WSA884x amplifiers arrives as one 32-bit sample
per speaker with Isense in the low and Vsense in the high 16 bits. The
VI module takes the halves in memory order, so the map must list
Isense first. With [1, 2, 3, 4] the module computes nonsense coil
resistance (4.7/3.7 Ohm instead of ~7.4 Ohm on Asus Vivobook S15).

Verified in factory test mode: [2, 1, 4, 3] gives 7.44 and 8.20 Ohm
against 7.35 and 7.57 Ohm R0 from the vendor calibration data.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 sound/soc/qcom/qdsp6/audioreach.c | 12 +++++++-----
 1 file changed, 7 insertions(+), 5 deletions(-)

diff --git a/sound/soc/qcom/qdsp6/audioreach.c b/sound/soc/qcom/qdsp6/audioreach.c
index 023c7b4..75fc909 100644
--- a/sound/soc/qcom/qdsp6/audioreach.c
+++ b/sound/soc/qcom/qdsp6/audioreach.c
@@ -1507,12 +1507,14 @@ static int audioreach_speaker_protection_vi(struct q6apm_graph *graph,
 		if (!mcfg->channel_map[i])
 			continue;
 		/*
-		 * Map speakers into Vsense and then Isense of each channel.
-		 * E.g. for PCM_CHANNEL_FL and PCM_CHANNEL_FR to:
-		 * [1, 2, 3, 4]
+		 * Each 32-bit feedback sample carries Isense in the low and Vsense
+		 * in the high 16 bits (WSA codec DMA V/I feedback), and the module
+		 * reads the halves in memory order. Map them to Isense and then
+		 * Vsense of each speaker, e.g. for PCM_CHANNEL_FL and
+		 * PCM_CHANNEL_FR: [2, 1, 4, 3]
 		 */
-		cm_cfg->cfg.channel_mapping[2 * j] = (mcfg->channel_map[i] - 1) * 2 + 1;
-		cm_cfg->cfg.channel_mapping[2 * j + 1] = (mcfg->channel_map[i] - 1) * 2 + 2;
+		cm_cfg->cfg.channel_mapping[2 * j] = (mcfg->channel_map[i] - 1) * 2 + 2;
+		cm_cfg->cfg.channel_mapping[2 * j + 1] = (mcfg->channel_map[i] - 1) * 2 + 1;
 
 		++j;
 	}
